# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA — never commit. IEEE-CIS is large and its licence does not permit
# redistribution. Committing it also bloats the repo permanently.
#
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. An unanchored `data/` matches a directory
# named `data` at ANY depth, which silently excluded the entire
# `src/fedguard/data/` package — synthetic.py, partition.py, features.py, the
# lot — from version control. Nothing errors: the files exist locally, tests
# pass locally, and a fresh clone simply cannot import fedguard at all,
# because experiment.py imports fedguard.data on line 39. The same applies to
# every directory rule below.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/data/
*.csv
*.parquet
*.npy
*.npz
!tests/fixtures/*.csv

# The dashboard's exported inputs are derived data, but the web app imports
# them statically, so a clone without them does not build.
!web/public/data/
!web/public/data/*.json

# Experiment outputs
/results/
/runs/
/artifacts/
*.jsonl
!tests/fixtures/*.jsonl

# Models
*.pt
*.pth
*.pkl
*.joblib

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Notebooks
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Env / secrets
.env
.env.local

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Node / Next.js (web surface)
node_modules/
.next/
out/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
.vercel

# Solidity / Hardhat (blockchain surface)
# Build output, regenerated by `npm run build`.
blockchain/artifacts/
blockchain/cache/
blockchain/typechain-types/
# Deployment records carry an address that is only meaningful on the machine
# and network that produced it - a committed localhost.json would point every
# other clone at a contract that does not exist there. Regenerate with
# `npm run deploy:local`. Committing a record for a shared testnet later would
# be reasonable; this rule is about the throwaway local one.
blockchain/deployments/
